<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market inactive - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market inactive - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said. Inquiry and demand was light. Feedlots very current.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed for the week to date on 104,200 head including 17,300 head or about 17 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>Confirmed - none   last week - none   last week - 22,500</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
